unication difficulty, egocentric, lack of learning orientation.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: arrogance, weak leadership.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Candidate B has stress resilience and technical, but uncooperative. Candidate A has technical but organization issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably Candidate C: reliability, decision quality, crew positive atmosphere outweigh communication issues? But difficulty communicating ideas could be serious for cockpit. However positive atmosphere suggests good crew cooperation despite communication difficulty? Might be contradictory.\n\nCandidate B: stress handling is crucial for long-distance. But uncooperative is a big concern for crew.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility and concentration are good, but arrogance and weak leadership may affect crew.\n\nCandidate A: technical competence but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nI think Candidate C seems most balanced: reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere. Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe can be mitigated with training. So I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: there is none yet, but we can say \"Given the facts we have, I propose...\". That's okay.\n\nProvide METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
